Thanks Eric,

I had created a factored observer variable for the key function and was also using this as a covariate for the MR model...  This did produce different p0 values for the primary and secondary observers but it obviously didn't have the desired outcome as the primary was given a lower detection rate than the secondary (0.29 and and 0.35, respectively). As you suspected, when I dropped the MRmodel covariates, the p0s were identical. I switched to the actual 'observer' variable for the MR model and all is well (p0 primary 0.80 and secondary 0.21).

I'm assuming that using a factored observer variable (text) in the key function shouldn't skew those results?

Thanks again,
Mitch Firman

