Hello,

I have a question about the standard error for the parameters when estimating a detection function in R. I know when using Distance in R, the parameter estimates are given on the log scale. For my own analysis with a hazard rate key function (no adjustment terms), I would like to report report the estimates and standard errors of sigma and b (not log(sigma) and log(b) ). My question is, what is the SE column in the ddf information reporting? Is it SE(log(sigma)) and SE(log(b))? If so, how to I obtain the standard error of sigma and b? For reference, this is the output from my model:

Detection function parameters
Scale coefficient(s):
            estimate        se
(Intercept) 2.330206 0.2733554

Shape coefficient(s):
            estimate        se
(Intercept) 0.677233 0.2835995

Thank you much,
Elaine

